Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/DMRedstone/rkllm-runtime
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Suggests: cmake, g++, pkg-config, libopencv-dev
Description: RKLLM runtime and OpenAI-compatible model service for Rockchip NPU
 This package ships the Rockchip RKLLM runtime for deploying large language
 models on Rockchip NPU devices (RK3588/RK3576/RK3562/RV1126B): the shared
 library librkllmrt.so, the C/C++ header, CMake and pkg-config integration
 files, board tuning scripts and the upstream example sources.
 .
 It also installs /usr/bin/rkllm as the single command entry point for both
 local inference and the HTTP service:
   rkllm chat <model>     interactive local chat
   rkllm run  <model> ..  one-shot inference
   rkllm serve <model>    OpenAI-compatible API (rkllm-server.service)
   rkllm list / info / selftest / config
 .
 The serve path runs the rewritten service stack: a FastAPI HTTP layer with
 Bearer authentication, an isolated inference subprocess with supervision and
 automatic restart, and memory budgeting that downgrades the context length
 before refusing to start. Configuration lives in /etc/default/rkllm-server
 (RKLLM_* variables); "rkllm config show" prints every key with its effective
 value and source, "rkllm config docs" prints the full key table.
 .
 Models are not included: compile them from HuggingFace checkpoints with the
 RKLLM toolkit on an x86 host first. The runtime needs the rknpu kernel driver
 that your board image provides; this package never ships or builds it.
 .
 Documentation is installed under /usr/share/doc/@PACKAGE@/ and the example
 sources under /usr/share/@PACKAGE@/examples/.
